// Credits & Methodology:
// This indicator implements Larry Williams' WillVal (Valuation) Index methodology,
// originally developed in 1990 for assessing overvalued and undervalued conditions
// in commodity markets. The WillVal Index measures current price relative to
// historical price action to identify potential overbought/oversold conditions.
//
// Key aspects of Larry Williams' methodology:
// - Uses dual exponential moving averages to create momentum oscillator
// - Normalizes results to 0-100 scale using historical range
// - Compares asset valuation against correlated securities
// - Default 156-period lookback represents ~3 years of weekly data
//
// This implementation extends the original methodology with:
// - Multi-security correlation analysis
// - Adaptive threshold calculation
// - Custom alert system
// - Enhanced visualization options
//
// Reference: Williams, Larry R. "Long-Term Secrets to Short-Term Trading"
// For more information on Larry Williams' complete methodology, refer to his published works.

